WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:15.300
What’s happenin, y'all? This week, we bendin over for da man with "The Handmaid’s Tale," by Margaret Atwood.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:23.720
The sh*t’s gone ham up in da USA, where a crew of Bible-thumpin honkies brought down da government,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:28.580
took a sh*t on the constitution, and now they runnin da game wit a new society called Gilead.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:34.740
And up in G-town, da man always hatin on women. They can't own property, work, learn, nothin.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.800
They just get tossed in a house and gotta do whatever they told.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.940
And since mutha Earth been f**ked by pollution, syphilis, and all kinda other mess,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.860
most women can’t pop out babies no mo. To keep da human race alive,

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:51.260
some women are captured and turned into Handmaids — which are basically baby-makin sex slaves.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.700
This story followin da life of Offred.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.060
Girl tried to bail to Canada wit her fam, but she got got by da fuzz and brought to da Reeducation Center,

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.380
where they gonna brainwash her into a true-blue handmaid.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:06.260
Offred eventually becomes da handmaid for some brotha named Commander Fred,

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:12.740
who she gotta get buck nasty wit while layin on his wife, Serena. And ain't nobody enjoyin themselves at all.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:18.200
What Serena don’t know though, is dat da Commander and Offred been chillin like she mo than jus his booty call.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.620
They doin da kinkiest things you can think of — scrabble and magazine readin. Mmm-mmm!

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.620
Offred ain't really feelin their little date nights, but she go along with it anyway.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:34.580
One day, Offred out shopping with a sista named Ofglen when she like "Psst — say girl, keep this on the DL, right?

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:39.340
But I'm a member of da resistance called "Mayday" and we tryna stick it to them Gilead haters.”

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.380
Pissed dat a bitch ain't gotten preggers yet,

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:46.520
Serena say she'll give Offred info on her long-lost daughter if she bangs the gardener, Nick.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.520
Serena wanna get rid of Offred real bad.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:54.300
Turns out, diddling Nick’s dangle is pretty sweet, and they start bangin on da reg.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:02:00.280
Later, Offred get word dat Ofglen offed herself cuz she was afraid da secret police were comin to get her.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:04.980
When Serena found out dat Offred hittin da club wit her hubby, girl gets mad crunk.

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.180
Not long after, two bustas roll up in a van to take Offred away.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:13.900
But, Nick say, “Don’t trip, girl. They actually Mayday members comin to save yo ass."

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.140
So, Offred get tossed in dat van, not knowin whether she bout to be freed or get wrecked.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.540
Da book end wit a section called "Historical Notes."

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:25.480
Bout two centuries later, some stuffy-ass professor talkin bout Gilead,

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.620
and da fact dat "The Handmaid’s Tale" might be a bunch of bullsh*t.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:30.960
Da hell?

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.060
Now, if you dun peeped dis text, you might be askin yourself —

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:39.840
Why da hell is this story all janky and out of order?

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:43.220
Da main character, Offred — even though dat ain't her real name —

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:47.540
tellin this story like she time trippin or somethin. Well there’s a good reason for that, homeboy.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.260
Like Offred herself tellin us,

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:56.340
"I'm sorry there is so much pain in this story. I'm sorry it's in fragments, like a body caught in a crossfire or pulled apart by force."

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.640
Da structure of dis novel is all jacked up, cuz that’s exactly how Offred feelin —

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.960
broken, tore up, and confused as hell as to how everything in da world went to sh*t.

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:09.160
Sure, Atwood givin us explicit reasons everything's so twisted —

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.740
like pollution and syphilis, but there’s more to it than that, padna.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:17.400
Think of dis book like a thought experiment, where Atwood takin common ignorant thoughts bout women,

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:22.040
like “women should stay in their place,” and show us where dat kinda hateful thinkin can lead us.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.260
When you got a whole society tryna put women in a box like that,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:30.800
it gonna make em into empty, choiceless drones dat don't serve no purpose other than poppin out babies.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:36.100
Sh*t, you can peep dat dehumanizing effect by the fact that Offred ain't even got a real name.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.120
Girl feelin like she already dead.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:45.200
"All the people I could love are dead or elsewhere... They might as well be nowhere, as I am for them. I too am a missing person."

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.720
In the end, everything looks like it turned out aight. Or does it?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.860
We get some uppity professor yappin bout Offred’s story like it's da distant past.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:58.400
But on da real, he usin da same kinda woman-hatin logic, sayin dat her story probably ain't even legit.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.240
And that's the same whack-ass jive dat turned the USA in to Gilead.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.780
So truth is, this book just straight-up depressing as hell.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.140
But chin up, homeboy, cuz dat subscribe button is still there to cheer yo ass up.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.960
So, hit it and catch me next week, playas. Peace.

